team_fallback:
  current: single_lead_with_pr_review_gate
  reason: PR tooling works, so `CHG-003` went through PR #1 and `T10` went through PR #2. Pushing over SSH still fails with `Permission denied (publickey)`; the HTTPS remote URL works. No subagent actor review was requested for this change; human review on the PR is the merge gate.
  chg_003_outcome: PR #1 "Run one mutation evaluation end to end (CHG-003)" merged 2026-07-30; two independent actor reviews during its development, the second of which found a surviving promotion-integrity hole and returned do-not-merge before the `T11` fix
  t10_outcome: PR #2 "Hard-gate a candidate whose realization changed nothing (CHG-003 T10)" merged 2026-07-31 as `36d01f8` after human review; the code change had lead self-review only, no independent actor review, but was covered test-first and the failing acceptance test was observed reporting PROMOTE before the gate existed
  readme_rework_outcome: pushed directly to `main` as `d1b9a71` under explicit user authorization, no PR; lead self-review only, no actor or human review pass, no code changes
  lost_challenge: the T10 code change and the README rework did not receive independent actor review; the T10 change has automated acceptance and unit coverage, the README change is a docs-only edit
